#8001
"Entrance"
"Just behind you, as you enter, the massive gates loom to either side.  The

gates being great bulky things crafted from thick oak planks and strapped

together with heavy steel bands.  A great black iron portcullis is hanging

above, suspended by thick chains.  Before you lies a tunnel through the dark

stone.  At the end of the tunnel, a small courtyard can be seen.  The tunnel

walls are planed smooth, almost slick to the touch.  The stone overhead is

craggy and dark with recesses and what appear to be little slits.

"
""
