"gates"
"Massive planks of wood capped and banded with thick, heavy bands of metal. 

The planks have been layered, three thick, vertical and then horizontal, then

diagonal.  Each plank must be three inches thick and the layers are separated

by a sheet of steel.  Thick bands of steel wrap the planks at four heights,

the thickest bands in the center.

"
E
"portcullis"
"A great blackiron grillework, this portcullis is made of two inch thick bars. 

The bars have been interlaced and welded to create a mesh with six inch

openings.  The vertical bars end in barbed points, that would sink into the

sockets along the floor, penetrating anything in their way on the descent. 

Two massive chains support its weight.

"
