"trophies"
"These trophies come in all shapes, and sizes; from taxidermied elves to

polished dwarf skulls.  There are relics of lost kingdoms, crowns, sceptres,

and the like.  There are dark and deadly blades, evil glowing armors, and even

a stone that emits powerful light-safely subdued of course.  The most

magnificient trophy, a large marble statue of Lonil, said to have been stolen

from one of his most sacred of temples.

"
E
"pillars"
"The center pillar is carved into likeness of Temohpab, dark, foreboding, and

all powerful.  The three pillars closest to him are of Oyasuminsai, Shninkoki,

and Jack.  The remaining three pay tribute to Morkith, Xiroce, and Morr. 

Tribute is paid to the other dark gods in the form of small shrines and

tapestries around the chamber.

"
E
"tapestries"
"A very large tapestry, this work shows the Triumvirate.  Depicted in their

normal color, black, upon a background of the purest blood-red.  The Dark Gods

are overseeing a glorious massacre.  Elves, halflings, gnomes, dwarves, and

humans all perish under their watchful gaze, and the swords of their minions.

"
