#8011
"Shrine"
"The center of this chamber is dominated by a great block of obsidian, easily

eight feet wide and five feet tall.  Directly behind the stone, that can only

be called an altar, is a matched pair of curtains.  Tall, stark white, silk

curtains that bear upon them the mark of the triumvirate.  The room has an

ominous feel, like someone is watching you.  To either side of the altar are

big candelabra, providing enough light to make out the shape of the room, but

no details.

"
"Temohpab altar

