#8021
"Makalyn's Haven"
"Upon entering, you can make out the soft sound of flowing water.  The area is

very large, and richly decorated.  A large bed has been placed in the center

of the room, covered in crimson and black silks, clearly meaning to be the

focus of the area.  Four abstract paintings cover three of the walls, and an

easel has been set at a corner, with a fifth unfinished painting.  The fourth

wall is covered in red-hued wooden shelves that display various instruments. 

The only window to the room is covered in thick crimson velvet, meant to keep

most of the light out of the room.  Magical lighting, as well as candles keep

the room dimly lit, but easily adjusted.  Luxurious furs cover the floor,

keeping the cold stone beneath from touching bare feet.  A small fireplace

sits under one of the paintings, heating the entire area.

"
""
