#8031
"Marakata's Lair"
"Although there is no boundary between the two, the room is roughly divided

into two parts, a sleeping and living area in the northern half and a work

area in the southern half.  The sleeping are is furnished with a large but

very plain looking bed in the north east corner, a fireplace in the middle of

the north wall and a wardrobe in the north west corner.  Two chairs are

positioned facing the fireplace.  The only furniture in the southern half of

the room is a large desk in the south west corner with a tapestry behind it

and a blackboard alongside it.  Much of the remaining space is taken up by a

large pentagram inscribed on the floor.  Mystical seeming symbols are

delicately carved into the wall at various intervals, although whether for

enchantment or decoration is unclear.  The walls, ceiling, and floor are all

of polished stone.  In the centre of the east wall is a large ironwood door,

and evenly spaced across the west wall are three tall narrow windows, each set

with heavy ironwood shutters.

"
""
